{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data at Rest.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data at Rest.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"data at rest data at rest","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Data at Rest.md","fileName":"Data at Rest.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Data at Rest","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 22:39\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Cloud Security and Data Protection]] [[Everyday Cybersecurity Applications]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Security and Data Protection","Everyday Cybersecurity Applications","Data in Transit","Data in Process","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data at Rest.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data at Rest.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"data at rest data at rest","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Data at Rest.md","fileName":"Data at Rest.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Data at Rest","heading":"Data at Rest","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Data at rest is inactive or intermittently used data stored in a digital medium, including disks, cloud storage, backups, and archives. Its storage location may persist long after the application that created it has stopped running.\n\nProtection can include encryption, access control, retention limits, integrity verification, and secure destruction. Backup and archival copies must be included because protecting only the primary store leaves other copies exposed.\n\nThe source distinguishes stored data from [[Data in Transit]] and [[Data in Process]]. At-rest protection can combine encryption with access control, but key management remains critical because a protected store becomes readable wherever its decryption keys are exposed.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Security and Data Protection","Everyday Cybersecurity Applications","Data in Transit","Data in Process","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data at Rest.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data at Rest.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"data at rest data at rest","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Data at Rest.md","fileName":"Data at Rest.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Data at Rest","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[cloudcomputing_mit.epub]]\n\n[[cybersecurity.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Security and Data Protection","Everyday Cybersecurity Applications","Data in Transit","Data in Process","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}